* The ending

# Moral movement and external result are independent axes. Crossing them gives
# six endings, and picking the cell is more precise than picking "happy" or
# "sad".
#
#            | Gets the Desire         | Does not get it
#  Rise      | Complete victory        | Moral victory, external defeat
#  Fall      | Wins and it is no use   | Complete tragedy
#  Resistance| The world proves him right | He pays the full price
#
# If you choose Resistance, the thirteen non-negotiables do not read the same.

- Moral movement ::
  # Rise / Fall / Resistance
- Opening Stance → closing Stance ::
- External result ::
  # Gets the Desire / does not get it
- What that crossing proves about the Theme ::

